{"BlockedEmail.should_block? increments match_count and updates last_match_at during validation, causing stats to be inflated when user records fail to save due to other validation errors or when valid? is called multiple times": 0.7693179249763489, "The regex in email_in_restriction_setting? is missing an end-of-string anchor ($\\z), allowing emails like user@company.com.evil.org to incorrectly match whitelist entry for company.com": 0.780901312828064, "BlockedEmail.should_block? uses case-sensitive comparison on PostgreSQL, allowing users to bypass email blocks by using different letter casing (e.g., SPAM@example.com bypasses block on spam@example.com)": 0.8679617047309875}